/*
 * insuranceCodes.js - the hospital's insurance company table (736 codes) from
 * the CPSI inscomp1 list.
 *
 * CODES ARE CASE-SENSITIVE. This table contains 21 pairs that differ only in
 * case and mean different payers - DCg is Humana Women's Clinic while DCG is
 * Lake Village Rehab Family Clinic. Every lookup goes through util.findByCode,
 * which matches the code exactly before it will consider any fallback.
 *
 * PAYER CATEGORY ASSIGNMENT
 * -------------------------
 * The source list gives a code and a plan name, not a payer category, so the
 * categories below were derived from the names by this rule set, applied in
 * order:
 *
 *   blank name, "DO NOT USE", "DELETE IN"   -> disabled, category Unknown
 *   private pay                             -> Self-pay
 *   Medicaid, MSCAN, PASSE plans            -> Medicaid
 *   Medicare Advantage plan names           -> Medicare Advantage
 *   Medicare supplement / Medigap / AARP    -> Medicare FFS (Medicare is primary)
 *   Medicare, Palmetto GBA                  -> Medicare FFS
 *   TRICARE / CHAMPVA / VA                  -> Other (military and veterans)
 *   workers compensation carriers           -> Other
 *   COVID HRSA, disability determination,
 *     hospice, grant and programme payers   -> Other
 *   everything else                         -> Commercial/Managed Care
 *
 * THIS IS A STARTING POINT, NOT AN AUTHORITY. Rows whose category was inferred
 * rather than stated carry a `note` saying so, and the Rules & codes screen
 * shows how often each code actually appears in the loaded data so the ones
 * that matter can be checked first.
 *
 * The Medicare FFS and Medicare Advantage rows deserve the most scrutiny: they
 * decide the IMM, MOON, and two-midnight review lists (docs/VALIDATION.md,
 * step 1). Medigap in particular is a judgement - the plan is a supplement, but
 * the primary payer behind it is Medicare fee-for-service, which is what makes
 * the patient notice-eligible.
 *
 * Codes marked "do not use" ship DISABLED rather than omitted, so one appearing
 * on a current account is reported as a retired code rather than as an
 * unrecognized one.
 */
